# CertusQA — Where to build (surface placement)

Use this whenever the user asks for dashboards, pages, UI, demos, or “put it on the website.”

## Surfaces

| Surface | Path | Visibility | URL | Put here |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Engine | `~/qa-forge-core` | Private | n/a | `qa/ai/core/**`, adapters, publish scripts, offline demos under `demo/` |
| Marketing | `~/certusqa-site` | **Public** | `certusqa.com` | Public landing, DeployShield, showcase — outcomes only |
| Ops console | `~/certusqa-app` | **Private** + Cloudflare Access | `app.certusqa.com` | Private dashboards, evidence viewers, internal tooling UI |

Business/ops docs stay in `~/QA_Package` (offer, runbooks, funnel — **not** a product UI host; no Cloudflare Pages app UI here).

When editing this rule, keep copies identical across: `qa-forge-core`, `certusqa-site`, `certusqa-app`, `QA_Package`.

## UI / dashboard requests

- **Private product UI** (ops dashboards, pack browsers, sprint views, judgments panels) → **`~/certusqa-app` only**
- **Public marketing pages** → **`~/certusqa-site` only**
- **Engine behavior / gate logic / fixture publishers** → **`~/qa-forge-core`** (e.g. `npm run publish:app-fixtures`); never ship `qa/ai/core/**` into site or app

If the Cursor workspace is `qa-forge-core` but the ask is a private dashboard, still implement under `~/certusqa-app` and say so.

## Hard boundaries

- Never copy `qa/ai/core/**` into `certusqa-site` or `certusqa-app`
- Never add nav/footer links from public `certusqa.com` to `app.certusqa.com`
- Ops console data = sanitized **fixture JSON** (or future API), not live engine imports
- Gate verdicts in the app are **precomputed at publish time** in `qa-forge-core`; the app displays them

## Good prompt shape (for the user / agent)

```text
In ~/certusqa-app, add a private page for <goal>.
Data: fixtures/ (or name the evidence pack).
Show: <specific tiles/lists>.
Do not: engine source in app; no link from certusqa.com.
```

## After UI changes in certusqa-app

Commit/push `certusqa-app` so Cloudflare Pages redeploys. New evidence → publish from engine:

```bash
cd ~/qa-forge-core
npm run publish:app-fixtures -- <evidenceDir> --id <pack-id>
```

Then commit/push updated `fixtures/` in `certusqa-app`.
